<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Voluntii</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of north-east Ireland recorded by Ptolemy, often identified with the Ulaid who gave their name to Ulster.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Voluntii, or Uoluntii, appear in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150 on the east coast of Ireland north of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/eblani">Eblani</a>, in the region of modern Counties Louth and Down. Their name is widely thought to be an early form of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ulaid">Ulaid</a>, the people whose name survives in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/northern-ireland">Ulster</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers or institutions in classical sources. If the identification with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ulaid">Ulaid</a> is correct, they were the forerunners of the people whose heroic traditions, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emain-macha">Emain Macha</a>, are preserved in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulster-cycle">Ulster Cycle</a> of Irish literature, though these tales were written down many centuries later.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The Voluntii vanish from classical sources after Ptolemy. In early medieval Ireland the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ulaid">Ulaid</a> formed the Kingdom of Ulaid, gradually pushed east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-bann">River Bann</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/voluntii.jpg" alt="Voluntii" width="320" height="408"><figcaption>Image: Erakis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ireland900.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Uoluntii</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=voluntii" aria-label="Voluntii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4665 336 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Voluntii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4985 592h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4985 592h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=voluntii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

